From 510caf9a8672e77fbf63e2d00fc23bed7cb4775f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiruba <koko0909e@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:51:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Widget rotation, vertex colors, a bounding pane and user data

- Widget::rotation (degrees, clockwise) and transformOrigin (also the
  center of renderScale; defaults keep the old behavior). Rotation is
  drawn through a Renderer2D transform and hit tests and pointer input
  undo it, so rotated buttons and sliders still work. Clipping inside a
  rotated widget uses the rotated bounding box.
- Vertex colors: four corner colors multiplied into a widget's own
  drawing (images, backgrounds, text), via Renderer2D corner colors.
- UIBoundingPane: draws nothing, emits Click (clickMessage) when pressed.
- Widget::userData: free "key=value" lines for scripts
  (GetUserData / GetUserDataFloat / HasUserData).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
